WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.940
Speaker 1: going back to Cuba momentarily.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.220
David, what should Joe Biden do about Cuba?

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.620
That's a very American centric way to ask
the question, and I think it's important to

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.589
start with first.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:19.020
Joe Biden doesn't necessarily have to do anything
about Cuba in the sense that the United States

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.910
doesn't have to be involved in every issue
in every country.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.910
That's a starting point.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.380
That's not isolationist.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.290
That's we we just we don't have to be involved
everywhere all the time.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.290
Now, you might say.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.070
Hold on a second, David.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.040
The U.S. is already involved in Cuba because
of the embargo and for other reasons.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.210
It's already entangled.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.239
And I would agree with you 100 percent.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.649
And we'll get into that in a second.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:43.699
But the first point is reframing.

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:48.859
Joe Biden doesn't have to do anything about
what's going on in any particular country

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:56.710
by definition now, because part of why Cuba
is the way it is today, part of.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:02.539
Is related to the American embargo of Cuba,
at absolute minimum, Joe Biden should be getting

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:05.280
rid of the amped up sanctions that Donald
Trump put in.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.030
Barack Obama had eased those sanctions.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.590
Donald Trump had reinstated some of those.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.650
Joe Biden should immediately step back from
those.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.680
At the same time, the U.S. simply cannot and
by cannot I mean, should not it's a moral

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.990
question, should not be involved in any kind
of influence.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:27.500
Campaign for regime change in Cuba, American
involvement in regime change in Central Latin

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.500
and South America.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.390
However, you want to slice and dice that region
of the world has been almost exclusively a

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.390
disaster.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.159
And there are so many, so many stories of
that.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:42.250
You can look at Columbia, you can look to
a lesser degree in Argentina, Nicaragua, Honduras.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.859
I mean, there's just so, so many questions.

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:51.130
So my preference would be because, remember,
I'm a progressive, anti authoritarian.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.829
My tendencies are not fascist, my tendencies
are not authoritarian.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:55.829
They're not dictatorial.

00:01:55.829 --> 00:01:58.780
I'm a small l progressive libertarian.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.420
I can't support any regime that's been in
power since nineteen fifty nine and that was

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.909
handed from one brother to another.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:07.689
It doesn't matter if what it was replacing
was bad.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:12.709
It doesn't matter if it was, if it was replacing
something that was supported by the US in

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:13.709
the fifties.

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:19.020
I'm a progressive libertarian so it's a there
are certain principles that are really important.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.190
And one is I don't support dictatorial regimes,
police states, etc.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:31.290
So the US should not support the Castro regime,
but should have zero involvement in regime

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.940
change operations.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.050
But beyond that, I don't know that I'm hugely
inclined to say the U.S. should have a bigger

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.050
and bigger role.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.739
I would love to see U.S. aid leveraged and
used.

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:47.870
Other nonprofit groups are eager to helping
Cuba make it easier for them to do that.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.580
Send food aid, send medical aid.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:54.590
I know some people say Cuba doesn't need any
medical aid, but they do.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:55.810
They do.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:03:00.989
But beyond that, I am very skeptical of American
involvement in Cuba because it has been pretty

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:03.599
disastrous for a long time.

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.910
If you I know it bums me out, but there are
some authoritarian leftists.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.910
Are they really leftists?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:10.910
I know.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.910
I know that that's a question you will ask.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:16.000
But there are some self-described leftists
who are authoritarian in my audience who have

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.409
a different perspective on Cuba.

00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:20.370
They really like the Castro regime.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.920
It's tough for me to find common ground with
that because I just can't support any kind

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.110
of autocratic police state type regime that's
lasted sixty years.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.280
I just I just can't do it.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.129
I can't you know, I don't support that in
North Korea.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.430
I don't support it.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.829
It's shorter and different.

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:38.840
But in Venezuela and I don't support it in
Cuba either.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.840
Send me your thoughts.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.790
What should or should not Joe Biden be doing
in Cuba?

